<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">National Salvation Front (Romania)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1989">1989</a>–<a href="/years/1992">1992</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The National Salvation Front was the body that took power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a> during the revolution of December 1989, after the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicolae-ceausescu">Nicolae Ceaușescu</a>. Led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ion-iliescu">Ion Iliescu</a> and dominated by former communists, it turned itself into a political party and won the elections of May 1990 by a wide margin, but its use of miners against protesters in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bucharest">Bucharest</a> in June 1990 drew criticism. It split in 1992.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/national-salvation-front-romania.jpg" alt="National Salvation Front (Romania)" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Traced by Stannered · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Romania_(1989_revolution).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
